---
title: "Heating Systems I"
code: "AIR-154"
category: "a-c-and-refrigeration"
credits: "3"
prerequisites: []
corequisites:
  - "2026/AIR-231"
corequisiteNote: "Corequisite: AIR 231"
---

Introduces types of fuels and their characteristics of combustion; types, components and characteristics of burners, and burner efficiency analyzers. Studies forced air heating systems including troubleshooting, preventive maintenance and servicing. Lecture 2 hours. Laboratory 2 hours. Total 4 hours per week. Additional course fee applies.
